{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted","id":314454,"title":"Lunar is Moon Exalted @_@ I thought they are Animal Exalted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-17T07:09:06-08:00","id":314454,"title":"Lunar is Moon Exalted @_@ I thought they are Animal Exalted","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/3R3u4rr.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Fighting Terrestrial by moonlight~! Fucking animal by daylight~! Getting horny from a real fight~!<br /> We are the Erotic Moon Terror~!</b><br /> <hr /></div><br /> <br /> I love the moon which mean Lunar should be rad as hell when I heard about Exalted, but then I read their boob and for some weird reasons, it is filled with so Goddamned much animal stuffs instead of moon-theme powers, shapeshifting into animal, animal charm's fluff, animal charm's name, spirit animal, totem animal, animal Tell, sex with animal, for the love of Kimbery, just stop it already, Artemis is not the only moon god around so seriously, just stop with the whole hunter-beast thing already.<br /> <br /> Since I find turning into animal boring, plus the fact that every Lunar spoiler so far has been about being terrorist and sabotage and animal and shapeshifting, none of which I want to base a character on, should I just go with a Moon-themed Exigent whose patron is one of Luna's subordinate ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 11-17-2014, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T07:42:11-08:00","id":314493,"title":"","content":"Okay.<br /> You have a moon themed Exigent and Lunar Exalted coming to make this thread all about them. How does this new Exalt defend themselves from such an onslaught?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T07:49:10-08:00","id":314498,"title":"","content":"There's a strong mythological association between animals and the Moon that's not quite reflected with the Sun, mostly because the sun has a strong association with humans; fire and light are associated with human civilization (cooking and forging), while darkness is associated with the wilds. Humans are diurnal, while many animals are nocturnal. The full moon drives people mad, robbing them of their human consciousness and reducing them to the level of beasts. Criminals act during the night, but criminals are generally considered subhuman.<br /> <br /> The problem with second edition Lunars is that they don't filter the association with animals through the mythological symbolism of the Moon. From what I gather, first edition Lunars <i>did</i> filter the association with animals through the mythological symbolism of the Moon, but completely failed at subtlety.<br /> <br /> What you want is a Lunar who presents a veneer of civilization to mask her beastial desires, much like the Moon reflects the Sun to provide a pale imitation of light. The Lunar slowly sheds the false light to reveal her true nature, just as the Moon reflects less and less light as it wanes, until the mask of civilization is completely gone and there remains only the hidden things in the dark, the beastial warform, and the hidden desires and vices that had thus far been suppressed. Once the Lunar's instincts are satisfied, she dons her disguise again and pretends everything was always perfectly normal. The Lunar does not shapeshift into animals; she shapeshifts into the darkness of the New Moon, symbolized by animals.<br /> <br /> Take, for example, Cersei Lannister, who acts like a perfectly regal queen most of the time, then turns around and fucks her brother when nobody's looking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T08:05:57-08:00","id":314510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a strong mythological association between animals and the Moon that's not quite reflected with the Sun </div> </div> </div>Again, there is other Moon God who is not Artemis, and pretty much every gods has an animal associated with them pretty much defeat the whole &quot;Moon = Animal&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay.<br /> You have a moon themed Exigent and Lunar Exalted coming to make this thread all about them. How does this new Exalt defend themselves from such an onslaught? </div> </div> </div>By the power of Love and Compassion seem like a good defense, it does work for the Buddha and Sailor Moon :cough:<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 11-17-2014, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T08:26:56-08:00","id":314540,"title":"","content":"Really the only got from your post is the Sailor Moon english theme-song running through my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T08:28:37-08:00","id":314541,"title":"","content":"That was actually a serious question about what this Moon Exigent would do, something that's far more interesting to me than another thread of people questioning the value of animal associations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T08:34:40-08:00","id":314543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted?p=314541#post314541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was actually a serious question about what this Moon Exigent would do, something that's far more interesting to me than another thread of people questioning the value of animal associations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking more moonlight powers like Eyes-as-Moonbeam Method, or stop enemy from hiding after you hit them since there is a shining mini moon floating above their head, eh, wait, now that I have to think about what he can do with his charms, this Exigent just sound more and more like Silver Solar...........hmmmmmmmmm.<br /> <br /> Maybe more Illusion and Misdirection power since Ex3 Lunar won't have those theme anymore, but how to make it more interesting looking than &quot;Your Illusion Glow Silver&quot; I wonder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really the only got from your post is the Sailor Moon english theme-song running through my head. </div> </div> </div>It was suppose to be &quot;Fly Me To The Moon&quot; at first, but I don't think Lunar and Jazz mix well at all. So I opted for Japanese Anime Opening J-Pop instead....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 11-17-2014, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T08:38:04-08:00","id":314547,"title":"","content":"Got to ask. what would the Lunar with the Moon emphasis charms be? Controlling the tide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T08:42:43-08:00","id":314548,"title":"","content":"A good way to avoid being a reskinned Solar is to figure out what their limitations are.<br /> <br /> To quote Holden on the difference between a Solar physician and a Chosen of Healing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Solar is not 'trying to be' anything. He is a physician-- since he's a Solar renowned for his medical acumen, let's say he's one of Creation's greatest physicians, in terms of skill. Because he's a Solar, that means he's going to be quite possibly the greatest doctor in the world, or certainly will stand among their ranks. That's what Solars are.<br /> <br /> Then let's say you have Argent Arrow, Chosen of Nala Ku, God of Healing and the Healer's Art. Let's say the Healer is an Ability-based Exalt. What this means is that he's going to be excellent in every aspect of healing within Medicine--as you'd expect! It also means that his Craft Charms are going to focus on mending what's broken, his Socialize Charms will focus on mending broken pacts and alliances, his Presence Charms will focus on restoring lapsed Intimacies or mending broken hearts, his Performance Charms will promote good health or the recollection of lost memories in those who hear them, his Resistance Charms will focus on rapid healing, his combat Charms may suck health out of enemies and give them to himself, or disarm an enemy's weapons the way a surgeon's scalpel might cut away infection, etc.<br /> <br /> The Solar's competence maxes out at &quot;can probably cure any ill.&quot; So will the Healer, possibly, because you don't uh, really get any better than that? This doesn't say anything about his mote costs or prereqs, of course, because we don't know how strong of an Exalt he is.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T08:52:25-08:00","id":314554,"title":"","content":"Interesting, so it's kinda like Sidereal Ride and Larceny where you intercept the word very literally. This mean that I have to find keywords that are associated with real-world Lunar deity and build the charmset around those keyword, plus give them some appropriate drawback (this seem like it'll be pretty hard, since hard drawback like Resonance and Paradox has been terrible so they are of no help, and soft drawing back like hole in the Infernal/Sidereal charmset has no clear guideline atm).<br /> <br /> I suppose everything will be clearer when Ex3 come, oooh, I create this thread to complain but got excited for Exigent instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T09:25:17-08:00","id":314622,"title":"","content":"Illusions might be a good way to go, Solars haven every really been super into those anyway. Little ones yes, but I'm talking big illusions, like a illusory ruined city in the woods or something that shreds apart in the daylight and becomes solid in the light of the moon, becoming a perfect illusion in the full moon or something. Being hidden and mysterious might be another way to take it, combat charms that rely on being unseen or misdirection. You could beat the crap out of a wyld hunt and leave them wondering who threw the first punch that started the brawl. <br /> <br /> Maybe dodge charms that let your opponent punch right through you, revealing that what they saw was merely a vision, Loki style. Being insubstantial, immaterial, as much a creature of thought as matter, maybe. That's not really how I see lunars, but could be how an exigent of the moon is. When a lunar is unseen it's not because he's barely material, he's disturbingly material, like a bear trap that you can't spot. A lunar wouldn't dodge by not being substantial, but by flowing like water around your attack, either metaphorically by moving like water or literally due to their protean nature. <br /> <br /> Not to say that lunars can't have illusion style charms, fucking dragonblooded have some of those, but it doesn't seem to me to be a super core lunar theme. Then again maybe that's just because they've been badly written in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T09:25:21-08:00","id":314623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted?p=314547#post314547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got to ask. what would the Lunar with the Moon emphasis charms be? Controlling the tide?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, just as it is, that's outside the realm of visceral self-change. Jen did mention Eyes-as-Moonbeams, though, which does seem like it would pass muster into EX3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T09:31:32-08:00","id":314627,"title":"","content":"Well the Moon was often a time telling piece, lunar calendars and so on so perhaps something to do with time and patterns, tides, and so on.<br /> <br /> From Wikipedia we've got (going for some of the less common Gods as Artemis has been name dropped already) Ataegina associated with spring and the ideas of rebirth, Jarilo again with life-death-rebirth as a cycle - with Jar as a root for Spring or Summer. Arianrhod takes part in myth to place three curses/geas on a boy (her son via humiliation) preventing him from the three things required of a man (name, arms, wife) so you;ve got a link between moon and curses. Heading east we get Chang'e who bestows beauty on her worshippers, Anumati is all over 'granting permission' which could be stretched again to link with the geas of Arianrhod as forbidding certain actions meaning the Moon could be associated with rules and permission to act. Chandra is known as 'one who illuminates the night' or 'bright drop' so we've got a light source connection as well as dew, fertility, plants and vegetation. Ay Ata is anotgher link to cyclic rebirth and death but also witchcraft, magic, evil spirits and demons only being consorted with at night. Africa gives us Khonsu associated with youth, life and travels as well as the passage of time as well as other names meaning embracer, pathfinder and defender. Mesoptamia gives us Sin with wisdom and astrology, Nikkal is associated with fruit. Mayan Xbalanque is a hero with many tales of bravery who eventually becomes the moon - their tales are often filled with trickery and skill overcoming monsters.<br /> <br /> So...plenty of options but common ones seem to be trickery, mystery, life-death-rebirth, time, travels, cycles, plants and fertility, cruses and magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T10:03:08-08:00","id":314662,"title":"","content":"Also Thoth who's the also the god of like all knowledge in addition to being the judge for the afterlife underworld stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/659-dominostro","name":"Dominostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar659_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T10:05:19-08:00","id":314664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted#post314454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but then I read their boob</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Lunar Perception Charm: Breast-Reading Understanding</b><br /> <br /> The primary mythic themes associated with the moon that come to mind for me are change and its associates, triple phases and life-death-rebirth, which Lunars already have pretty good. Trickery and mystery are kind of associated with that, but they're also part of the darkness aspect of the moon. Same with curses and magic; the idea is that the moon/night does all the underhanded stuff that upright solar heroes don't need to bother with, they just use their manly and virtuous fists. Beauty, especially with the adjective otherworldly, comes to mind. Thoth/Khonsu's lunar associations seem more the stuff that Exalted assigns to Sidereals, especially as concerns timekeeping and destiny stuff, but I'm hard-pressed to think of what else Lunar Intelligence looks like (as opposed to Perception or Wits).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T10:08:32-08:00","id":314667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dominostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted?p=314662#post314662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Thoth who's the also the god of like all knowledge in addition to being the judge for the afterlife underworld stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought Thoth was the god of manses and infrastructure-based play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T10:36:57-08:00","id":314673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted?p=314664#post314664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Lunar Perception Charm: Breast-Reading Understanding</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm watching Aesthetica of a Rogue Hero out of pure boredom and I got a kick out of that reply to a typo...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T10:36:57-08:00","id":314674,"title":"","content":"Doing some cursory research the moon is associated with themes much are reflection/mirrors, subtlety, transitions, cycles, renewal, passivity, emotion, intuition, psyche, wonder, shadows, nocturnal animals, madness, silver, fertility, clarity, purity, magic, mysticism, mesmerism, wisdom/hidden meanings. illumination.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, while generalizations of the moon being of a feminine quality, many cultures regard it as something very masculine.<br /> <br /> This also brings into idea of the possibilities of how Lunars do intelligence, intuition and hidden meanings, wisdom and clarity, than the blazing philsophical glory of Solars. They are more subtle in their workings, opening the mind to the esoteric.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":393,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","user":"Godjaw","date":". 11-17-2014, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T11:40:00-08:00","id":314728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted?p=314674#post314674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doing some cursory research the moon is associated with themes much are reflection/mirrors, subtlety, transitions, cycles, renewal, passivity, emotion, intuition, psyche, wonder, shadows, nocturnal animals, madness, silver, fertility, clarity, purity, magic, mysticism, mesmerism, wisdom/hidden meanings. illumination.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, while generalizations of the moon being of a feminine quality, many cultures regard it as something very masculine.<br /> <br /> This also brings into idea of the possibilities of how Lunars do intelligence, intuition and hidden meanings, wisdom and clarity, than the blazing philsophical glory of Solars. They are more subtle in their workings, opening the mind to the esoteric.</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of subtlety? Because the stated goal of being very visible doesn't seem very subtle, though I suppose the shapeshifting and enjoying no hint of being anything other than the shape might qualify.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T12:20:27-08:00","id":314748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted#post314454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I love the moon which mean Lunar should be rad as hell when I heard about Exalted, but then I read their boob and for some weird reasons, it is filled with so Goddamned much animal stuffs instead of moon-theme powers, shapeshifting into animal, animal charm's fluff, animal charm's name, spirit animal, totem animal, animal Tell, sex with animal, for the love of Kimbery, just stop it already, Artemis is not the only moon god around so seriously, just stop with the whole hunter-beast thing already.<br /> <br /> Since I find turning into animal boring, plus the fact that every Lunar spoiler so far has been about being terrorist and sabotage and animal and shapeshifting, none of which I want to base a character on, should I just go with a Moon-themed Exigent whose patron is one of Luna's subordinate ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Luna is called the many faced goddess because she's goddess of the moon Artemis has absolutely nothing do to with that in Exalted beyond basis in Exalted. She's seen taking many forms beyond that of just animals, she's a fickle goddess that changes her opinion on a whim, and is insanely in love with Gaia. She's also the Goddess of Trickery and Cunning for the most part, loving that her Exalted are able to think on their feet and use their abilities to work around obstacles. Her major inspiration being that the Moon changes faces and never keep to one form. <br /> <br /> Not sure where you're getting this idea that Luna = Artemis, but the fickle lady is far from being like her. Luna is a bit insane and doesn't care about people getting in her moonsilver pantaloons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T12:20:31-08:00","id":314749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted?p=314728#post314728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What kind of subtlety? Because the stated goal of being very visible doesn't seem very subtle, though I suppose the shapeshifting and enjoying no hint of being anything other than the shape might qualify.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Subtlety isn't necessarily stealth. It's rather the opposite, working in plain sight but still undetected.<br /> <br /> Subtle is their power, intrinsic to self and form in a way Solar power isn't. Their power effects their self, what they are, their Attributes. Solar power is the opposite of this, it works with what they can do, their Abilities.<br /> <br /> As for the moon it's subtle in it's workings on life and the world. It's push and pull marking the tides and life cycles. Such a strong influence from doing so little.<br /> <br /> Subtle in it's borrowed light. Allowing for illumination, and to look upon it's glory without being blinded. A metaphor for knowledge possibly?<br /> <br /> Subtle in it's changing face. A new one each night but remains the moon still.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T15:48:38-08:00","id":314880,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of the reason Lunars got their name and their main themes was from Werewolf: the Apocalypse, where you had many shapeshifting types that were spiritually bound by Luna into roles (auspices), that viewed Luna as the sister of their mother (Gaia) and where Luna's metal (silver) was their bane: their patron's strength is also their weakness. Yes, I'm ignoring the ones wholly or partially under Helios instead of Luna, but they are the vast minority.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted?p=314543#post314543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe more Illusion and Misdirection power <b>since Ex3 Lunar won't have those theme anymore</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. Why do you think this is going to be the case?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 11-17-2014, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T16:21:20-08:00","id":314895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted?p=314880#post314880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Emphasis mine. Why do you think this is going to be the case?</div> </div> </div> </div>Developer comments seem to state as much. The emphasis is very much rooted in physicality.<br /> <br /> Spoilered for space.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3 What We Know Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Q: (Mostlyjoe)</b><br /> What about other themes? Like Illusions, magic, what if I want to play a non-combat Lunar? Social, mysterious, etc? How thick is the support for that?<br /> <b>A: (John M\u00f8rke)</b><br /> Definite support for social, mysterious Lunars. Not so much illusions. A Lunar has the most majestic god-body ever. They are all about being seen.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RPG.Net &quot;Ask the Developers&quot; thread</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Q: MostlyJoe</b><br /> 8. Do you see Lunars gaining powers over the world in a style of Druids? Commanding beasts, the land itself? We have heard of Shamanistic magic being at their command, but I'm trying to understand what is the them of their magic in EX3 beyond shapeshifting. Gaia is their link to animal forms. Do they call upon her aid (or that of her children) to do their bidding? If they are Loki...how? Is Lunars being on the forefront of Sorcery and Necromancy with Solars still a thing?<br /> <br /> <b>A: <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?733370-Exalted-Ask-the-Developers/page333\" target=\"_blank\">hatewheel</a></b><br /> 8. Re: Druidism: Not really, no. Lunar magic is focused through their bodies. It is heavily based on shapeshifting and physicality. Not command of the world or command of reality, but command of self. Re: sorcery and necromancy: no, we have moved away from that vision.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T16:30:55-08:00","id":314903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted?p=314895#post314895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Developer comments seem to state as much. The emphasis is very much rooted in physicality.<br /> <br /> Spoilered for space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sigh. That's the sad part really. The &quot;I look like the person you expect to see/I look like the person you most want to see/I look like an Everyman in this crowd&quot; and the Butterfly Eyes stuff were the most interesting things in the Lunar Charmset. <br /> <br /> I hope they do cool stuff with Socials and Mentals because Full Moons hardly needed as much help being useful and interesting as the others did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T19:11:43-08:00","id":315003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted?p=314903#post314903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sigh. That's the sad part really. The &quot;I look like the person you expect to see/I look like the person you most want to see/I look like an Everyman in this crowd&quot; and the Butterfly Eyes stuff were the most interesting things in the Lunar Charmset.<br /> <br /> I hope they do cool stuff with Socials and Mentals because Full Moons hardly needed as much help being useful and interesting as the others did.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't see how this isn't still possible, except it's not an illusion. You quite literally shape into it than just create an image.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T19:20:59-08:00","id":315008,"title":"","content":"You can only be in one shape at a time, whereas the type of illusion Zel is talking about causes you to appear as different things to different people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T19:49:37-08:00","id":315025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted?p=314748#post314748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Luna is called the many faced goddess because she's goddess of the moon Artemis has absolutely nothing do to with that in Exalted beyond basis in Exalted. She's seen taking many forms beyond that of just animals, she's a fickle goddess that changes her opinion on a whim, and is insanely in love with Gaia. She's also the Goddess of Trickery and Cunning for the most part, loving that her Exalted are able to think on their feet and use their abilities to work around obstacles. Her major inspiration being that the Moon changes faces and never keep to one form.<br /> <br /> Not sure where you're getting this idea that Luna = Artemis, but the fickle lady is far from being like her. Luna is a bit insane and doesn't care about people getting in her moonsilver pantaloons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Artemis (and Diana) are moon-goddesses who have being a huntress first and foremost. They're deities of the hunt, of wild animals, of the untamed wilderness. Artemis is a nature-goddess, and at one point had a bear cult. When Zeus granted her wishes she asked for no city to be devoted to her, but rather to rule the mountains. Her symbols are her hunting dogs, her bow, the stag, and the moon. She is a virgin goddess who strikes down those who trespass against her, she turns those who offend her into animals or curses them to be attacked by wild beasts. She tricked the Aloadae, brothers who could only be slain by each other, by running in between them as a deer that they would spear one another. She saved the infant Atalanta, who was abandoned to die by her father, by sending a bear to suckle the baby, who was found and raised by hunters. The Spartans sacrificed to her before military campaigns, and she becalmed the sea to aid the Trojans when Agammenon refused to do the same. She was also a goddess of childbirth and fertility, prayed to by expectant mothers. She was associated with the wearing of masks, with hawks, with a golden chariot pulled by sacred deer.<br /> <br /> Luna took some heavy inspiration from Artemis and the many goddesses who fused in the region to form her, and their regional variants. She and Hecate (who was a competing deity in the region with similar attributes) are pretty much the roots of most Western moon-symbolism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T21:00:06-08:00","id":315049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted?p=315025#post315025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Artemis (and Diana) are moon-goddesses who have being a huntress first and foremost. They're deities of the hunt, of wild animals, of the untamed wilderness. Artemis is a nature-goddess, and at one point had a bear cult. When Zeus granted her wishes she asked for no city to be devoted to her, but rather to rule the mountains. Her symbols are her hunting dogs, her bow, the stag, and the moon. She is a virgin goddess who strikes down those who trespass against her, she turns those who offend her into animals or curses them to be attacked by wild beasts. She tricked the Aloadae, brothers who could only be slain by each other, by running in between them as a deer that they would spear one another. She saved the infant Atalanta, who was abandoned to die by her father, by sending a bear to suckle the baby, who was found and raised by hunters. The Spartans sacrificed to her before military campaigns, and she becalmed the sea to aid the Trojans when Agammenon refused to do the same. She was also a goddess of childbirth and fertility, prayed to by expectant mothers. She was associated with the wearing of masks, with hawks, with a golden chariot pulled by sacred deer.<br /> <br /> Luna took some heavy inspiration from Artemis and the many goddesses who fused in the region to form her, and their regional variants. She and Hecate (who was a competing deity in the region with similar attributes) are pretty much the roots of most Western moon-symbolism.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was pretty much what i was going to say. i would add to this that the moon rules over many of the cycles that exist within the natural world from sleep cycles (influenced by both solar and lunar cycles) to the tide, to the behavior of nocturnal creatures and including the psychology of human beings to some degree or another. and with it's heavy association with change and werewolf/lycanthrope lore, it's kind of a no-brainer why Lunars are so heavily animal themed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T22:10:41-08:00","id":315081,"title":"","content":"Chang'e, the Chinese moon goddess, also has an animal association (rabbits, specifically), as the ancient Chinese thought the spots on the moon look like a rabbit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T22:18:40-08:00","id":315084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted?p=315081#post315081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chang'e, the Chinese moon goddess, also has an animal association (rabbits, specifically), as the ancient Chinese thought the spots on the moon look like a rabbit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty hard to drawn inspiration from her though, since she's less moon goddess and more celestial maiden who lives on the moon. Hmmm, her stories are about immortal pill, the moon rabbits are also said to make those magic medicine on the moon surface (the Japanese said they made mochi for some reasons). The Hinduism moon god also has a connection to some kind of magic healing ambrosia so I can see some potential for a Medicine focus Exigent here.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, the Maya also think that there are rabbits on the moon.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T00:08:52-08:00","id":315099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted?p=315084#post315084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty hard to drawn inspiration from her though, since she's less moon goddess and more celestial maiden who lives on the moon. Hmmm, her stories are about immortal pill, the moon rabbits are also said to make those magic medicine on the moon surface (the Japanese said they made mochi for some reasons). The Hinduism moon god also has a connection to some kind of magic healing ambrosia so I can see some potential for a Medicine focus Exigent here.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, the Maya also think that there are rabbits on the moon.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Two candidates to be gods fought over becoming the Sun deity but one chickened out at the last moment while the other stepped forward, seeing that the first one stepped up as well. Then someone threw a rabbit at the first one and that damaged them so they shone less brightly. Because obviously.<br /> <br /> God I love myths. Where else do rabbits determine the brightness of a celestial body?<br /> <br /> An Exigent of the moon could happily be the beautiful mysterious wo/man who wields trickery, mysticism and magic or you could get a wise knowledgeable sage who uses that knowledge to deal with demons and dark spirits for the benefit of their followers/detriment of their foes or perhaps a master of cycles, time, patterns, the seasons, life-death-rebirth or maybe go down the route of geas and permission being an Exigent who determines law, enforces rules, grants gifts to allow others to succeed (granting permission) and laying curses (or geas) on those who displease them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T22:53:44-08:00","id":315956,"title":"","content":"I tripped over Scion Hero earlier today was reminded that it had a general-purpose Moon purview and that I need to stop leaving books on the floor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T00:18:53-08:00","id":315981,"title":"","content":"Is it just me or does the size and positioning of the censorship patch make Raksi's...?right? leg look more like a meaty tail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T10:43:44-08:00","id":317551,"title":"","content":"I was going to bring up Scion, as well; what are some of the powers it associates with the Moon gods? As I recall, shapechanging isn't part of it, that belongs to another purview entirely...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T14:06:31-08:00","id":317692,"title":"","content":"Scion's Moon purview is mostly about madness (which in Scion means Virtue Extremities, and in Exalted I guess means Limit), stealth, and general Solar-esque glory. There's also a sorcery-style travel in the form of a moon chariot, and a moon castle with alien butlers. My personal favorite is the one that lets you look out from the literal moon while it's in the sky. (It would be the one that uses a personal tiny moon as a shield, but that one actually kinda sucks.)<br /> There is a separate Animal purview which has the shapeshifting stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T08:05:42-08:00","id":318254,"title":"","content":"Well in order it\u2019s \u2013<br /> Smoking Mirror- for an eagle eye view<br /> Tidal Interference- gravity powers<br /> Phase Cloak- stealth power that emulates the phases of the moon<br /> Lunacy- what it sounds like!<br /> Eclipse Halo- blinding light<br /> Phase Body- like phase cloak but makes you partially intangible and thus harder to hit<br /> Moon Chariot- what it sounds like<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have Scion: God because Hero was fun then the power level of the game went to shit in Demigod and our game fell to pieces.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T09:49:44-08:00","id":318318,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=46AUvg8A02A\" target=\"_blank\">MoOOOOOoooOOOOOon!~</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T15:53:29-08:00","id":318545,"title":"","content":"I'm disappointed illusions seem to have been knocked out as Lunar thematic. <br /> <br /> However, based on the fairfolk book, the fact that moonlight causes them calcification seems like it might be a good Anti-Illusion or maybe stretched to Anti-Wyld or Anti-Magic theme.<br /> -Lunar emits a large burst of moonlight, removing all illusions in the area and wreaking havoc with fae-glamor.<br /> -Lunar strikes a magical construct, disrupting or destroying the magic sustaining it. <br /> <br /> Attraction/Gravity seems like a really good theme ripe for lots of charm action:<br /> -Lunar mentially attracts a person to them. As long as the lunar is in the direction of the path they travel, they will unknowingly pick paths that bring them towards the Lunar.<br /> -Lunar makes a more attractive target despite being surrounded by other better targets. Helps fulfill a guardian/defensive role. <br /> -Lunar pulls all sorts of physical gravity stunts, as long as the effects bring things towards the lunar. <br /> <br /> Moon is very associated with portals (Moon doors, In the setting the Moon s a sphere covered by many portals to many places, etc)<br /> Portals-Hopefully enough said.<br /> <br /> Sleep, dreams and nightmares, (rest?) seems like it may fall under the Moon auspices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4352-krellian","name":"Krellian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4352_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T16:30:17-08:00","id":318567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krellian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/314454-lunar-is-moon-exalted-_-i-thought-they-are-animal-exalted?p=318545#post318545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm disappointed illusions seem to have been knocked out as Lunar thematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there is a distinct difference between creating an illusion in the manner Fair Folk do and tricking people using subtle aspects of shapeshifting and misdirection. Maybe shapeshifting is going to be more integrated into the charmset; maybe some shapeshifting is going to take the exact place as some of the Illusion-keyword stuff that was previously in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T17:04:56-08:00","id":322267,"title":"","content":"Maybe you want another moon? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton's blog</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ululaya</b> <i>The Scarlet Moon, Empress of the Blood-Drenched Tide, Lady of a Thousand Faces</i><br /> Third and Fetich Soul of the Demon Sea<br /> Ululaya cometh in the form of a Lady of mutable Countenance, clad in scarlet Robes that glow like the Sunset. Hers is the power of the Tide, which maketh the great things Small and the small things Great. She giveth strength to the Weak, wealth to the Impoverished, beauty to the Hideous, sanity to the Mad, and morals to the Depraved. In like Manner she taketh away these things from those possessed of a Surfeit, leaving them hollow in their Absence. She also commands the tides of the Sea, that grindeth away Stones and sweepeth Ships into the Deep.</div> </div> </div> </div> It occurred to me recently that she seems to be what a lot of people want Luna to be. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T20:15:32-08:00","id":322376,"title":"","content":"Eh, but.........Demon can't grant Exigent exaltation to people....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.